## What this cycle added

The previous cycle had proved the source-normalization gate **red** for every taper whose transform decays only polynomially, and recorded — as an *assessment*, not a theorem — that the one remaining regime (exponentially decaying transform) is incompatible with the compact-support/plateau hypotheses under which the source-side `L⁶` Gram floor is proved. This cycle turns that into theorems and closes the regime the earlier argument left uncovered.

New module `RiemannAnalytic/TaperAnalyticIncompatibility.lean`:
- the holomorphic strip extension of an inverse Fourier transform (`invFourierExt`, `differentiableOn_invFourierExt`, `analyticOnNhd_invFourierExt`), with the supporting integrability facts;
