- `log_pow_le_mul_rpow` — `(log N)^k ≤ (k/δ)^k N^δ` for every `δ > 0`;
- `gate_fails_of_power_gain` — master theorem: any surviving positive power of `N` defeats the contraction condition, subject only to an explicit constant comparison;
- `taperedWeilMass_lower_of_expDecay`, `taperedWeil_gate_fails_of_subcritical_expDecay` — the gate fails for every subcritical exponential decay rate `r < 1/2` (the critical rate is exactly the archimedean normalization `n^{-1/2}`);
