The verdict is red for the taper class of the Gram floor in the polynomial and subcritical-exponential regimes, and the supercritical regime is proved empty for that class. Making "red" unconditional for *every* compactly supported taper still needs one ingredient that is not proved here: a lower bound for the prime-frequency mass of the transform (statement (ii) assumes a pointwise floor on the top window, while statement (i) excludes only a uniform upper exponential bound). This is stated explicitly as the next thing to prove in `RIEMANN_G16_REPORT.md`.

